{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">A same-named file forces a tradeoff between staleness and re-downloading it constantly. A content-hashed filename removes the tradeoff entirely.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Cache hashed assets forever with immutable; keep the HTML that references them on a short or no-cache lifetime so it always picks up the new hash.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">A service worker's own cache lifecycle doesn't inherit HTTP Cache-Control semantics, apply the same short-pointer/long-payload discipline to it deliberately if one is in play.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
